emergence is to me one of the most  exciting things that we can study in  science when patterns spontaneously form  in systems comprised of objects whether  they're atoms or molecules or or nano  particles or flocks of birds those  patterns are said to be emergent because  they're not evident by simply looking at  the individual constituents of the  system so for example when you look up  in the sky and you see these intricate  patterns that birds form when they're  when they're flying around those  patterns are nothing that you would have  guessed at if you just looked at the  birds and thought about how the birds  are flying next to one another or if you  take water and you freeze it into ice in  the freezer or you make a solution of  data particles and outcomes a  complicated photonic structure you would  never have guessed just by looking at  individual water molecule or individual  nanoparticles what those structures  would look like and so emergence  underlies so many different types of  questions in science from the kind of  traffic jams that you get from the  interactions of many cars in the roads -  even the origin of life and how complex  structures emerged from simpler  structures in my group we study  emergence by making mathematical models  of different kinds of systems and then  we solve these models using computers  usually very large very fast computers  and what's what's important about using  the computer is that we're able to strip  away one by one all the kinds of  interactions that might be present in a  system so that we can see the role of  all of the different interactions and  one of the contributions to emergence  that that my students and I are  particularly fascinated by is is the  idea of entropy entropy is typically  thought of as disorder and so the idea  that entropy can actually contribute to  order is sometimes surprising to people  but in fact entropy can be the cause of  emerge  and in many different different systems  and so that is something that's really  interesting to us
 

